  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5002.12 Explosive",
  "priorExpiration": "2005-01-10",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5002.12 “Explosive” means any chemical compound, mixture, or device, the primary or common purpose of which is to function by explosion and includes, but is not limited to:\n\n(a) Dynamite;\n\n(b) Black powder;\n\n(c) Pellet powder:\n\n(d) Initiating explosives;\n\n(e) Detonators;\n\n(f) Safety fuses;\n\n(g) Squibs;\n\n(h) Detonating cord;\n\n(i) Igniter cord;\n\n(j) Igniters; and\n\n(k) Display fireworks.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 5000) #6055, eff 7-1-95, EXPIRED: 7-1-03\n\nNew. #8117, INTERIM, eff 7-14-04, EXPIRED: 1-10-05\n\nNew. #8261, eff 1-21-05; ss and moved by #9765-A, eff 8-2-10 (from Saf-C 5002.09); renumbered by #12124 (from Saf-C 5002.11); ss by #12738, eff 4-30-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5000.html"
